## The finding

`crime_00070` — **Duplicate Component Shape** (medium, confidence 0.70), one `<div>` subtree repeated across 4 files:

| File | Lines |
|---|---|
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |
| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |
| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |

I read all four sites. The subtree is byte-identical except for one string — the submit label:

```tsx
<div className="mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4">
  <Link
    href="/dashboard/invoices"
    className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
  >
    Cancel
  </Link>
  <Button type="submit">Create Invoice</Button>   {/* or "Edit Invoice" */}
</div>
```

That's the drift surface: the cancel-link class string is 9 utility classes repeated 4×, and the `href` is hard-coded 4×. Any change to button height, hover colour, gap, or the cancel destination has to land four times, and there is no test covering any of them (`test_gap: 0.5`).

**One caveat on scope:** `final-example/` and `starter-example/` are two separate Next.js apps — each has its own `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and `@/*` alias. There is no import path between them, so a single component cannot serve all four call sites without introducing a shared workspace package. The honest fix is **one component per app, 2 call sites each** (the cross-app half of the duplication is the tutorial's before/after pair and is intentional). I've written the plan that way; the shared-package variant is at the end if you want all four.

## Files that would change

**New (2):**
- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/form-actions.tsx`

**Edited (4)** — each drops its 9-line footer subtree and its now-unused `Link` import:
- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (142–150)
- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (152–160)
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` (101–109)
- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` (112–120)

`Button` stays imported by `form-actions.tsx` rather than each form. Note the forms are `'use client'`; `FormActions` itself has no state or handlers, so leave it a Server Component and let the client boundary stay where it is.

## Proposed component

`app/ui/form-actions.tsx` — sits next to `button.tsx`, not under `invoices/`, because the shape is a generic form footer (login-form has the same visual problem, though it isn't in this finding).

```tsx
import Link from 'next/link';
import { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';

export type FormActionsProps = {
  /** Destination for the cancel link. Required — no default route baked in. */
  cancelHref: string;
  /** Submit button content. Required: it is the only thing that differs today. */
  submitLabel: React.ReactNode;
  /** Cancel link text. */
  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;      // default: 'Cancel'
  /** Disables submit — for useFormStatus pending states. */
  disabled?: boolean;
  /** Extra actions rendered left of Cancel (e.g. a Delete Invoice button). */
  children?: React.ReactNode;
  /** Escape hatch for one-off layout overrides; merged, not replaced. */
  className?: string;
};

export function FormActions({
  cancelHref,
  submitLabel,
  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',
  disabled,
  children,
  className,
}: FormActionsProps) {
  return (
    <div className={clsx('mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4', className)}>
      {children}
      <Link
        href={cancelHref}
        className="flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200"
      >
        {cancelLabel}
      </Link>
      <Button type="submit" aria-disabled={disabled}>
        {submitLabel}
      </Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

**Public API summary**

| | Name | Type | Required | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| prop | `cancelHref` | `string` | yes | routing, not layout — the one thing a caller must own |
| prop | `submitLabel` | `ReactNode` | yes | the only value that varies across the 4 sites today |
| prop | `cancelLabel` | `ReactNode` | no (`'Cancel'`) | i18n / "Discard" wording |
| prop | `disabled` | `boolean` | no | `useFormStatus` pending state |
| prop | `className` | `string` | no | merged onto the container; caller can't drop the base classes |
| slot | `children` | `ReactNode` | no | leading actions — the obvious next need is a destructive **Delete** on edit-form |

**Slots vs. props rationale:** exactly one slot (`children`), positioned left of Cancel. `submitLabel` is typed `ReactNode` rather than `string` so an icon or spinner composes without a second slot, but it is *not* a full submit-button slot — keeping `<Button type="submit">` inside the component is what makes the shape enforceable. Nothing here parameterises the class strings; the whole point is that they stop being caller-visible.

## Call sites after

```tsx
// final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx
<FormActions cancelHref="/dashboard/invoices" submitLabel="Create Invoice" />

// final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx
<FormActions cancelHref="/dashboard/invoices" submitLabel="Edit Invoice" />
```

## Verification

Re-run `crimes scan --format json` on the fixture: `crime_00070` should drop out entirely (all 4 occurrences resolved, or 2 if you do one app). Findings `crime_00090/91/94/95` (Design Token Escape) live in the same four files but anchor to lines 36–100 — the radio-input `px` values, untouched by this change; expect them to survive.

## Two things this deliberately doesn't fix

- **All four sites in one component** would need a `packages/ui` workspace shared by both apps — a build-system change, not a refactor. Say the word if you want that instead; the component API above is unchanged, only the import path moves.
- The higher-`agent_risk` neighbours in these same files are the status literals: `crime_00051` (`"status"` across 5 files) and `crime_00071`/`crime_00072` (`"pending"`/`"paid"` compared in 4 files across 2 expression shapes). Those are policy duplication, not shape duplication, and want a `isPending(invoice)`-style helper rather than a component — separate change.
